Adapted on 20 Nov 2026 (SPEC ATSC-07, ATSC-08):

- apps/backend/app/services/ats.py `compute_ats_score`: a score part that can't
  be measured returns None and the score is rescaled over the parts that were
  measured; the role title graded 100 in the headline, 75 in the summary,
  otherwise by word overlap. WERA: services/agent/wera_agent/nodes/ats.py
  (`ats_score`, `title_grade`).
- apps/backend/app/services/text_match.py `keyword_in_text`: a keyword matches
  only with no word character touching it. WERA:
  services/agent/wera_agent/domain/vocab.py (`_alias_re`).
- apps/backend/app/services/refiner.py `analyze_keyword_gaps`: missing keywords
  split into those the master CV can supply ("injectable") and those it can't,
  and the match the CV could reach. WERA: nodes/ats.py (`compare`) and
  apps/web/app/review/_components/ReviewRail.tsx.
- apps/frontend/components/builder/jd-comparison-view.tsx and
  apps/frontend/lib/utils/keyword-matcher.ts: the job description beside the
  CV with keywords highlighted, longest first, a stats bar with the match
  percentage, and colour bands at 80% and 60%. WERA:
  apps/web/app/review/_components/JobVsCv.tsx and highlight.ts.

Changes were made: the scoring parts, weights, matcher (synonym groups,
case-sensitive and ambiguous aliases) and interface are WERA's own.

